# 13. FIRESTORE SECURITY AND DATA PRIVACY

Security is mandatory.

Extend existing Firestore security rules rather than replacing them.

### User-owned information

Only the authenticated owner should be able to:
- Read private preferences.
- Change private preferences.
- Read private watchlist data.
- Edit personal anime progress.
- Manage private collections.
- Manage personal recommendation feedback.
- Edit dashboard configuration.

### Public collections

Public collections may be readable by authenticated users or the appropriate audience, subject to the selected visibility.

Only the owner can modify them.

Private collections must never be readable by other users.

### Validation

Validate:
- Authenticated ownership.
- Document ownership.
- Allowed field names.
- Data types.
- String lengths.
- Numeric ranges.
- Status values.
- Visibility values.
- Valid timestamps.
- Collection entry ownership.

Prevent users from changing owner IDs.

Prevent users from writing another user's preferences or watchlist.

Do not trust the client to enforce security.

### Privacy controls

Provide:
- Disable personalised recommendations.
- Clear recommendation feedback.
- Reset personalisation settings.
- Delete individual anime tracker entries.
- Delete personal collections.
- Export personalisation data where feasible.

A full account deletion workflow is not part of this build unless one already exists. Do not introduce an incomplete deletion mechanism.

